          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "puzzle, you get the answer to Rakesh’s second puzzle. That is, the first number is 7 and the second is 18!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.138,
            0.316,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.166,
            0.847,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us try to find a few more pairs of numbers from their sums and differences:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.214,
            0.472,
            0.234
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "(a) \\  Sum  = 27,  Difference  = 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.214,
            0.796,
            0.234
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{(b)~~Sum=4,~Difference=12}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.239,
            0.472,
            0.259
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{(c)} \\quad \\mathrm{Sum} = 0, \\quad \\mathrm{Difference} = 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.239,
            0.81,
            0.259
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{~(d)~~~Sum~=~0,~Difference~=~-10}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.264,
            0.485,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(e)\t Sum = – 7, Difference = – 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.264,
            0.823,
            0.284
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{~(f)~~~Sum~=~-7,Difference~=~-13}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.296,
            0.848,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose a partner and take turns to play this game. In each turn, one of you can think of two integers, and give their sum and difference; the other person must then figure out the integers. After some practice, you can perform this magic trick for your family members and surprise them!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.414,
            0.417,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carrom Coin Integers"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.446,
            0.847,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A carrom coin is struck to move it to the right. Each strike moves the coin a certain number of units of distance rightwards based on the force of the strike."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.502,
            0.774,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.227,
                0.502,
                0.774,
                0.597
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.612,
            0.847,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ To begin with, the coin is at point 0. If the coin is struck twice, with the first strike moving it by 4 units and the second strike moving it by 3 units, what will be the final position of the coin?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.682,
            0.654,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is clear that the coin will be 4 + 3 = 7 units from 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.719,
            0.847,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? If the coin is struck twice, and if the two movements are known, can you give a formula for the final position of the coin?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.772,
            0.537,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the first strike moves the coin "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units to the right and if the second strike moves the coin ‘b’ units to the right, then the final position is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { P } = a + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where P is the distance of the coin from the starting point 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.564,
            0.77,
            0.866,
            0.874
